# The player page is a client-side route in a single-page app with no router,
# so the server has to hand /play/<code> the same index.html and let the app
# read the path.
#
# Scoped to /play/* rather than a blanket /* fallback: everything else should
# still be able to 404 honestly, and /api/* is served by Functions, which run
# before this file is consulted.
#
# The destination is "/" and not "/index.html": Pages strips `/index` and
# `.html` from paths, so a rule pointing at /index.html is detected as an
# infinite loop and silently dropped. Root serves the same document.
/play/* / 200
